1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,845
Adapt the lab contract to maintenance requests
while preserving validation, human review, and

2
00:00:05,915 --> 00:00:07,366
auditable decisions.

3
00:00:07,436 --> 00:00:10,231
State the key uncertainty and prediction first.

4
00:00:10,301 --> 00:00:13,842
Implement only the smallest
complete path that addresses it.

5
00:00:13,912 --> 00:00:19,736
Then apply the constraint card: an integration
is unavailable and external model calls are

6
00:00:19,806 --> 00:00:25,673
prohibited. Demonstrate the permitted fallback
and explain which evidence remains unavailable.

7
00:00:25,743 --> 00:00:31,268
Your implementation may use rules or an
approved optional model, but the comparison must

8
00:00:31,338 --> 00:00:33,493
justify any added complexity.

9
00:00:33,563 --> 00:00:36,315
The integration fails just before the review.

10
00:00:36,385 --> 00:00:39,243
A local fixture preserves the input contract.

11
00:00:39,313 --> 00:00:44,711
It demonstrates review behavior but cannot
establish live integration reliability.

12
00:00:44,781 --> 00:00:46,807
Your decision record should say both.

13
00:00:46,877 --> 00:00:51,656
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

14
00:00:51,726 --> 00:00:57,827
Submit working code, test evidence, a timestamped
prediction, and a revised decision after the

15
00:00:57,897 --> 00:00:58,964
constraint.

16
00:00:59,034 --> 00:01:05,349
The fallback uses synthetic fixtures, validates
asset identifiers, flags urgent text for the

17
00:01:05,419 --> 00:01:08,107
supervisor, and saves reviewed decisions.

18
00:01:08,177 --> 00:01:10,459
Prediction and evidence remain separate.

19
00:01:10,529 --> 00:01:16,311
The record names live integration as untested
and preserves the original safety boundary.

20
00:01:16,381 --> 00:01:21,543
A good submission explains why these controls
address the case rather than merely listing

21
00:01:21,613 --> 00:01:22,659
features.

22
00:01:22,729 --> 00:01:24,862
What must the fallback report preserve?

23
00:01:24,932 --> 00:01:27,492
A. The claim that integration passed B.

24
00:01:27,562 --> 00:01:29,738
Only the favorable screenshots C.

25
00:01:29,808 --> 00:01:33,243
The distinction between
tested and untested behavior.

26
00:01:33,313 --> 00:01:34,721
The best answer is C.

27
00:01:34,791 --> 00:01:37,009
Fallbacks change the evidence boundary.
